  "notes": "A current CompTIA A+ certificate is an industry-recognized certification that examines a student's understanding of the information technology landscape. Certificate holders will have met qualifying skills in IT hardware, operating systems, computer networking, mobile devices, visualization/cloud computing, security, and systems troubleshooting. Due to the ever changing objectives of the CompTIA exams, students should hold a current CompTIA A+ certification with exam scores posted within the last 6 years for the current or previous exam version. For more information about this certification, visit https://comptia.org/certifications/a.",
